@* SPEC:  docs/02-LipiTabs-Spec.md §3 (LipiTab parameters)
   PHASE: 2.6.1 — Layout components
   AMEND: Phase 2.6.3 Stage 2 — registration loop fix
   AMEND: CHANGE-LOG.md A21 — "two Optional mechanisms" mitigation
          (XML-doc accuracy fix + env-gated Optional-on-non-Vertical guard)

   LipiTab is a pure parameter carrier + self-registrar.
   It renders NO markup. LipiTabs reads registered tabs and renders
   the tablist buttons + panels.

   Registration flow:
     1. LipiTabs wraps ChildContent in <CascadingValue Value="this">
     2. LipiTab receives the parent via [CascadingParameter]
     3. LipiTab generates a stable resolved key once (OnInitialized)
     4. LipiTab calls parent.RegisterTab() in OnInitialized
     5. LipiTab calls parent.UpdateTab() in OnParametersSet — ONLY when
        a meaningful parameter actually changed (dirty-check pattern,
        prevents infinite re-render loop with the parent's StateHasChanged).
     6. LipiTab calls parent.UnregisterTab() in Dispose (tab removed)

   Phase 2.6.3 Stage 2 — what changed and why:

   PRIOR BUG: OnParametersSet unconditionally called Parent.UpdateTab(...).
   UpdateTab called StateHasChanged() on the parent, which re-rendered the
   CascadingValue, which re-set parameters on every LipiTab child, which
   re-fired OnParametersSet, which re-called UpdateTab — infinite loop.
   With 4 children × 3 LipiTabs instances on the Layout demo page = 12
   loop participants saturating the thread pool before the circuit could
   complete its first render.

   FIX: Two layers of defense.
     (1) Here in LipiTab: cache previous parameter values in OnInitialized.
         OnParametersSet computes new values and only calls UpdateTab when
         a value genuinely changed. ChildContent is excluded from the check
         (Razor regenerates RenderFragment delegates on every render even
         when content is identical, so reference comparison would always
         report "changed" and defeat the dirty-check). The LATEST ChildContent
         delegate is always passed through, just without triggering a rerender.
     (2) In LipiTabs.UpdateTab: even if UpdateTab is called, compare the new
         registration against the existing one via HasSameParameterValues and
         skip StateHasChanged when truly unchanged. Belt-and-braces.

   Auto-key generation: previously lived as a static counter in
   LipiTabRegistration which generated a NEW key on every BuildRegistration
   call for tabs without Key. That meant UpdateTab/UnregisterTab could never
   find existing entries (different ResolvedKey each call). Auto-key now
   lives on the LipiTab INSTANCE, generated exactly once in OnInitialized,
   reused for every subsequent BuildRegistration call. Stable per instance.

   ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   TWO "OPTIONAL" MECHANISMS — read before touching Optional or TabState.Optional

   LipiTab expresses optionality through TWO intentionally separate mechanisms.
   They are NOT duplicates and must not be merged or "deduplicated":

     • bool Optional             → Vertical variant ONLY. Inserts a section
                                   divider in the rail before this tab. Inert
                                   (no visual effect) in Underline and Pill.

     • State = TabState.Optional → The dashed-border colour treatment. Renders
                                   the dashed border in the Underline variant;
                                   treats the tab as stateless (no state dot)
                                   in Vertical. Ignored by Pill.

   The "optional" cue is variant-specific: Vertical shows it as a divider
   (bool Optional), Underline shows it as a dashed border (State=Optional).
   A developer who sets bool Optional on an Underline/Pill LipiTabs gets
   nothing — so OnInitialized throws in Development (env-gated guard below)
   to surface the mistake instead of failing silently. Full rationale and the
   decision record: docs/02-LipiTabs-Spec.md and CHANGE-LOG.md A21.
   ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*@

@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Hosting
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging
@implements IDisposable
@inject IWebHostEnvironment Env
@inject ILogger<LipiTab> Log

@* No markup — parent LipiTabs handles all rendering *@

@code {
    // ==========================================================================
    // PARENT CASCADE
    // ==========================================================================

    [CascadingParameter] private LipiTabs? Parent { get; set; }


    // ==========================================================================
    // IDENTITY
    // ==========================================================================

    /// <summary>Stable string key for this tab. Used by LipiTabs for
    /// @bind-ActiveTab binding and for panel/button aria wiring.
    /// Auto-generated ("tab-{8-char-guid}") if not provided.
    /// Must be unique within the same LipiTabs instance.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Key { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Visible label text. Required. Used as aria-label + tooltip
    /// in IconOnly Vertical mode where the text is visually hidden.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string Label { get; set; } = string.Empty;


    // ==========================================================================
    // VISUAL
    // ==========================================================================

    /// <summary>Lucide icon name (e.g. "user", "map-pin", "clipboard").
    /// Optional for Underline and Pill. Required when parent LipiTabs
    /// has IconOnly="true" (Vertical variant).</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Icon { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Validation/completion state. Drives colour treatment
    /// (underline colour, label colour, state dot). Ignored on Pill variant.
    /// Default: TabState.Default — neutral, no signal.
    /// <para><see cref="TabState.Optional"/> is the dashed-border "optional content"
    /// cue — distinct from the <see cref="Optional"/> bool below, which is the
    /// Vertical-rail section divider. See this file's header ("TWO OPTIONAL
    /// MECHANISMS") and docs/02-LipiTabs-Spec.md.</para></summary>
    [Parameter] public TabState State { get; set; } = TabState.Default;

    /// <summary>Count badge shown next to the label (e.g. "3 pending").
    /// Null = no badge shown. Zero renders as "0" — use null to hide.</summary>
    [Parameter] public int? Count { get; set; }


    // ==========================================================================
    // BEHAVIOUR
    // ==========================================================================

    /// <summary>Vertical variant ONLY — inserts a section divider in the rail
    /// before this tab, visually grouping it as optional/secondary. Has NO
    /// visual effect in the Underline or Pill variants; setting Optional="true"
    /// on a non-Vertical LipiTabs throws in Development (env-gated guard in
    /// OnInitialized).
    /// <para>This is NOT the dashed-border treatment. For the dashed-border
    /// "optional content" cue, set <see cref="State"/> to
    /// <see cref="TabState.Optional"/> instead. <c>Optional</c> (divider) and
    /// <c>State=TabState.Optional</c> (dashed border) are intentionally separate
    /// mechanisms — see this file's header ("TWO OPTIONAL MECHANISMS") and
    /// docs/02-LipiTabs-Spec.md.</para></summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Optional { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Prevents selection. Tab button has aria-disabled + cursor:not-allowed.
    /// Panel content is not rendered regardless of RenderMode.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Disabled { get; set; }


    // ==========================================================================
    // CONTENT
    // ==========================================================================

    /// <summary>Panel content rendered when this tab is active (Lazy) or
    /// mounted but hidden (Eager). Required — a tab without content is an error.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }


    // ==========================================================================
    // INSTANCE STATE (Phase 2.6.3 Stage 2)
    // ==========================================================================

    // Stable resolved key — generated once in OnInitialized, reused thereafter.
    // For tabs without an explicit Key parameter, we generate "tab-{8charguid}".
    // 8 chars of a Guid is ~32 bits of entropy — plenty for distinguishing tabs
    // within a single LipiTabs instance (collision probability vanishingly small).
    private string _resolvedKey = string.Empty;

    // Snapshot of parameter values from the previous registration build.
    // OnParametersSet compares new values against these to decide whether the
    // parent's UpdateTab actually needs to fire. ChildContent is excluded
    // (RenderFragment reference changes every render — see LipiTabRegistration
    // for rationale).
    private string?  _prevKey;
    private string   _prevLabel    = string.Empty;
    private string?  _prevIcon;
    private TabState _prevState;
    private int?     _prevCount;
    private bool     _prevOptional;
    private bool     _prevDisabled;


    // ==========================================================================
    // LIFECYCLE — registration + cleanup
    // ==========================================================================

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        if (Parent is null)
            throw new InvalidOperationException(
                "LipiTab must be a direct child of LipiTabs. " +
                "Wrap your LipiTab components inside <LipiTabs>.</LipiTabs>.");

        // ── Env-gated guard: bool Optional is Vertical-only ─────────────────
        // See the "TWO OPTIONAL MECHANISMS" note in this file's header. `Optional`
        // inserts a section divider in the Vertical rail and has NO effect in the
        // Underline or Pill variants. A developer reaching for `Optional` on a
        // non-Vertical LipiTabs almost certainly wants the dashed-border treatment
        // — which is a different mechanism: State="TabState.Optional".
        //
        // Env-gated pattern (mirrors LipiButton A14 / LipiInputBase.ValidateOrFallback):
        //   Development → throw, so the developer sees it during build/test
        //   Production  → log + continue (the flag is simply inert; rendering is
        //                 unaffected, so there is nothing to "fall back" to)
        // OnInitialized-scoped deliberately: Variant changing at runtime is not a
        // supported pattern for LipiTabs, so a once-per-instance check is sufficient.
        if (Optional && Parent.Variant != TabsVariant.Vertical)
        {
            var message =
                $"LipiTab '{Label}': Optional=\"true\" has no effect on the " +
                $"{Parent.Variant} variant — it only inserts a section divider in the " +
                "Vertical rail. For the dashed-border optional treatment, set " +
                "State=\"TabState.Optional\" instead. Optional (divider) and " +
                "State=TabState.Optional (dashed border) are intentionally separate " +
                "mechanisms — see docs/02-LipiTabs-Spec.md.";

            if (Env.IsDevelopment())
                throw new InvalidOperationException(message);

            Log.LogError("[LipiTab] {Message}", message);
        }

        // Resolve the key exactly once. If Key was provided, use it; otherwise
        // generate a stable instance-scoped auto-key. Subsequent BuildRegistration
        // calls reuse this value so UpdateTab/UnregisterTab can find existing
        // entries.
        _resolvedKey = !string.IsNullOrEmpty(Key)
            ? Key!
            : $"tab-{Guid.NewGuid().ToString("N").Substring(0, 8)}";

        // Seed previous-parameter snapshot to current values so OnParametersSet
        // (which Blazor calls once on first render AFTER OnInitialized) sees
        // "no change" and doesn't double-fire UpdateTab on top of RegisterTab.
        SnapshotCurrentParameters();

        Parent.RegisterTab(BuildRegistration());
    }

    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        if (Parent is null) return;

        // Dirty check — only call UpdateTab when a meaningful parameter changed.
        // Breaks the OnParametersSet → UpdateTab → StateHasChanged →
        // CascadingValue re-render → OnParametersSet infinite loop.
        //
        // KNOWN LIMITATION (Phase 2.6.3 Stage 2):
        // ChildContent is excluded from the dirty check, so this also means
        // if a tab's ChildContent captures dynamic page state (a value that
        // changes outside the tab), the stored registration's ChildContent
        // delegate will become stale and the panel will render with the
        // CAPTURED-AT-REGISTRATION value, not the current one. This is fine
        // for static panel content (the Layout page demo, the PatientNew tabs
        // each managing their own state internally). It would be a problem
        // for a tab whose panel content directly references a page-level
        // counter or other dynamic value — which is an uncommon pattern.
        // If this limitation bites in practice, the fix is architectural
        // (move panel rendering from parent's registration list to each
        // LipiTab's own render output) and deserves its own design pass.
        if (!HasMeaningfulParameterChange()) return;

        SnapshotCurrentParameters();
        Parent.UpdateTab(BuildRegistration());
    }

    public void Dispose()
    {
        // _resolvedKey was set in OnInitialized — guaranteed non-empty if we got here
        if (Parent is not null && !string.IsNullOrEmpty(_resolvedKey))
            Parent.UnregisterTab(_resolvedKey);
    }

    private bool HasMeaningfulParameterChange()
        => Key      != _prevKey
        || Label    != _prevLabel
        || Icon     != _prevIcon
        || State    != _prevState
        || Count    != _prevCount
        || Optional != _prevOptional
        || Disabled != _prevDisabled;

    private void SnapshotCurrentParameters()
    {
        _prevKey      = Key;
        _prevLabel    = Label;
        _prevIcon     = Icon;
        _prevState    = State;
        _prevCount    = Count;
        _prevOptional = Optional;
        _prevDisabled = Disabled;
    }

    private LipiTabRegistration BuildRegistration() => new(
        resolvedKey:  _resolvedKey,
        key:          Key,
        label:        Label,
        icon:         Icon,
        state:        State,
        count:        Count,
        optional:     Optional,
        disabled:     Disabled,
        childContent: ChildContent);
}
